A parity cross-check found the matrix advertising surfaces Forge never generates.
Tier 1 makes each claim TRUE (deliver) or honestly not-yet-delivered (downgrade),
without building the heavy renderers (tracked under kernel epic 90f2f631).

DELIVERED
- MCP: wire Cursor project-local .cursor/mcp.json (setupCursorMcpConfig, mirrors
  Claude) via the tested renderer; read→merge→write preserves user servers and the
  JSONC data-loss guard carries through. displayMcpStatus reports both auto-wired
  (dropped the manual "Configure via Cursor Settings" hint).
- skills/stages: Cursor unproven→native (.cursor/skills IS populated at setup);
  add S10 Cursor Agent Skills source. Hermes native→forge-owned and the stage-graph
  now reflects reality (Forge writes .hermes/skills/<stage>; no more "no per-stage
  file" contradiction). Codex labels fixed: .codex/skills is the staging mirror,
  install target is $CODEX_HOME/skills.

DOWNGRADED (honest not-yet-delivered, each pointing at tracked kernel work)
- hooks: no harness-native hook is rendered — all enforcement is git hooks. claude/
  codex native→contract-only; cursor unsupported→not-delivered (.cursor/hooks.json,
  Cursor 1.7+). Fixed the S1 skills-doc miscitation. (kernel 988ae187)
- agents/subagents: whole domain unimplemented → every harness not-delivered/
  unsupported; added to AGENT_SKILL_PARITY future-work. (kernel 802aa4d8)
- typedMemory: write-only (insights.js), no projection renderer → all 4 rows
  not-delivered. (kernel dce9da46)
- codex mcp: Codex reads GLOBAL $CODEX_HOME/config.toml, not project-local →
  not-delivered at project setup. codex .agents/skills repo discovery (55dfeccf).

GUARDS + CLEANUP
- STATUS_VOCABULARY enum + a test asserting no row uses an off-vocabulary (dishonest)
  status; removed 'unproven'/'skill-backed'.
- Dropped directories.rules + copyRules from claude.plugin.json (no more empty
  never-populated .claude/rules on setup); kept .claude/rules in the D20 scanner via
  STATIC_INSTRUCTION_ROOTS so bd-retirement coverage is preserved.
- Fixed the stale agents-config.js generateCursorConfig comment; corrected the parity
  doc's Cursor instructions column to AGENTS.md; regenerated the D20 artifact.

Tier-2 follow-ups tracked under kernel epic 90f2f631 (children 55dfeccf/988ae187/
802aa4d8/dce9da46/1e68255c).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
